mod lexical_reject_unclosed_string;

// A string literal whose closing quote never comes. The literal runs to the
// end of the file, taking everything after its opening quote, the annotations
// below included, so an unclosed literal is one per file and it has to be
// last. The diagnostic is at the opening quote.
//
// The parser then reaches the end of the file with the statement unfinished
// and reports the missing ';' there, a follow-on. The literal is a global so
// that is the only one: inside a function the unclosed block would add a
// second, and two diagnostics at the end of the file cannot both be annotated
// on its final line.
//
// Nothing after the opening quote may hold a double quote, or it would close
// the literal: that is why the annotations carry no quoted message.

imm greeting = "never closed;  //~ ErrorBadTok:16
//~ ErrorNoSemi follow-on
